    "title": "PSM Icehouse hosts annual high school hockey media day - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Glenn Marini ,\n58 minutes ago\nFORT WAYNE, Ind. (WANE) – The 51st season of high school hockey in Fort Wayne is gearing up for league play as PSM Icehouse hosted its annual media day on Wednesday.\nTwo local teams won a state title last season, as the Fort Wayne Vipers claimed the 1A crown while Carroll earned the 4A state championship. For the Vipers, it was their second straight state title, having won the 2A title the previous season. Carroll, meanwhile, won the 4A crown in dramatic fashion by besting state powerhouse Culver Academy 3-2 in triple overtime.\nCarroll has also been king of the rink locally, as the Chargers have won back-to-back league Memorial Cup playoff championships and have not lost a league game since the city title game in 2023 – a stretch of 34 games.\nWhile some area teams have played non-league games, the first night of league play is Saturday October 18, and the first Wednesday night of league games is October 22.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WANE 15.",
